'''Effingham station''' is an [[Amtrak]] intercity train station in [[Effingham, Illinois]], United States. The station contains three houses, at the [[CSX Transportation|CSXT]] [[St. Louis Line Subdivision]] (ex-[[Pennsylvania Railroad]]) crossing that once served Amtrak's former ''[[National Limited (Amtrak train)|National Limited]]'' line between [[Kansas City, Missouri|Kansas City]] and either [[Washington D.C.]] or [[New York City]] until 1979. The station is a [[flag stop]] on the ''[[City of New Orleans (train)|City of New Orleans]]'' route, served only when passengers have tickets to and from the station; the {{lnl|Amtrak|Illini/Saluki}} also stops here.

